# Test

Inspect the project's test framework and existing conventions. Select tests covering important behavior and failure cases; avoid testing implementation details. Run appropriate commands where authorized, record actual exit status and describe skipped checks. Never claim a test passed without running it.

Examples: add a regression case for a bug; run targeted tests after a feature. If the framework cannot run, report the error and other evidence available.
